BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Nerikomi with Eiko Maeda | Nov 14 & 15 2026 | Dupont
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261212
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261212
UID:parkdale-10381209436443@parkdalepottery.ca
DESCRIPTION:Date & Times: - Option 1: Saturday\, November 14 & Sunday\, No
 vember 15\, 2026 - NEW Option 2: Saturday and Sunday Dec 12 and 13 - 9:00a
 m – 4:00pm - 1 Hour Lunch break on each day. Instructor: Eiko Maeda Loca
 tion: 300 Campbell Avenue\, Unit 115 Join us for a two-day workshop with c
 eramic artist Eiko Maeda\, exploring the traditional Japanese technique of
  Nerikomi. Unlike surface decoration\, Nerikomi builds pattern directly in
 to the clay body itself\, layering\, stacking\, and folding differently co
 loured clays until intricate designs run through the material from edge to
  edge. Over two days\, you'll learn to prepare and condition coloured clay
 s\, build your own pattern blocks and work through four distinct pattern d
 esigns\, each resulting in a finished ceramic piece approximately 15 cm in
  diameter. Eiko will guide you through every stage\, from initial slab to 
 shaped\, refined form. This workshop is open to makers at all levels. No p
 rior experience with Nerikomi is required\, though some familiarity with h
 and-building is an asset. ABOUT EIKO MAEDA Eiko Maeda trained in Japanese 
 lacquer at Joshibi University of Art and Design in Tokyo before discoverin
 g ceramics after relocating to Canada. She has spent over a decade develop
 ing and teaching her Nerikomi practice from her studio in Ontario\, and ha
 s been recognized by the Ontario Arts Council and the Toronto Outdoor Art 
 Fair. In 2026\, her work was exhibited in Taipei\, Taiwan. PLEASE NOTE Fir
 ing is included in the registration fee. Finished works will be available 
 for pick-up approximately 3–4 weeks after the workshop concludes. You wi
 ll be notified by email when your pieces are ready. All Specialty tools wi
 ll be available for usage with the option to purchase your tools at the en
 d of the course.
